# Logbook — {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}} (append-only; the full narrative record)

The complete, permanent history of the campaign: one entry per experiment, in order, **verbatim and
never trimmed**. The runner (`scripts/run_campaign.py`) **auto-appends the facts** of each entry; the
agent **completes the narrative slots** (Analysis, Expected-vs-found, Verification, Excluded-data, NEXT) of that same entry right after.
This archive is what lets `results/JOURNAL.md` stay a short steering view.

**Rules — read these once, then never read the rest of this file:**
- **Append only — never touch a PAST entry.** New entries are appended at the bottom (automatically, by
  the runner). You complete the narrative of the **current** entry; once you move to the next experiment,
  no earlier entry is ever edited, compressed, reordered, or deleted (including disputes, negative
  results, and refuted findings).
- **Never read this file in full.** It grows without bound, and loading it whole would bloat the working
  context — which defeats its purpose. Consult it only by **targeted search** (grep for an exp id or a
  term) or by reading a **specific slice** when you genuinely need an old detail.
- **Entry format:** a `## <exp_id> - <label> - <UTC>` header, then **one bold-labelled field per line as a
  bullet** — `- **Hypothesis**: …`, `- **Predicted**: …`, `- **Change**: …`, `- **Result**: …` (auto-filled
  by the runner), then `- **Analysis**: …`, `- **Expected vs found**: …`, `- **Verification**: …`, `- **Excluded data**: …`, `- **Disputes & responses**: …`,
  `- **Status**: …`, `- **Artifacts**: …`, `- **NEXT**: …` (the agent completes). **Keep each field on its
  own bullet line — never collapse them into one paragraph** (a single newline renders as a space in
  Markdown, so separate bullets are what make the entry readable).
- The numbers live in `scoreboard.tsv`, settled findings in `DISCOVERIES.md`, the navigation map in
  `INDEX.md`; this file is the full *narrative*.

**Completing the current entry** (fill the slots the runner left blank, before moving on):
- **Analysis** — inside the predicted range? guardrail hold? ceiling-move vs gap-to-ceiling? statistical
  vs systematic? real win or overfit?
- **Expected vs found** — the one-line gap between what you predicted and what you got (the gap is the
  insight): matched / above / below, and by how much. When they diverge, that divergence is the finding —
  name it, don't smooth it over.
- **Verification** — the `{{VERIFY_SKILL}}` verdict: CONFIRMED / PROVISIONAL / QUESTIONABLE ASSUMPTION /
  REFUTED / INCONCLUSIVE, with key evidence.
- **Excluded data** — any run or data point you dropped from this experiment's analysis, each with its cause
  (a legitimate reason like "solver hit its iteration cap", never "looked wrong"). **Append-only, never
  silent:** a silent drop is indistinguishable from cherry-picking (never manipulate the evaluation).
  Investigate the anomaly before discarding — it may be the result. Leave `none` when nothing was excluded.
- **Disputes & responses** — every issue raised by the verifier OR the user, each with your response;
  never delete one (rebut if you disagree). Format:
  `date — raised by <verifier|user>: <issue> → response: <agree + fix | counter-argument>`.
- **Status** — confirmed | PROVISIONAL (rests on an adapted eval) | QUESTIONABLE ASSUMPTION (shaky
  premise) | open.
- **NEXT** — the orthogonal lever to try next.

